HorizonKV — anonymous research artifact

This artifact adapts inference code from Self-Forcing and Wan2.1, whose
repository licenses are Apache-2.0. The adapted
`wan/modules/causal_model.py` also carries a CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 file-level notice.
Changes include sparse KV retrieval, bounded GPU/host
storage, overlap execution, residency-aware configuration selection, and
portable inference/experiment entry points. Modified source files carry a
notice. Model parameter names remain compatible with public checkpoints.

Third-party attributions refer to public dependencies, not submission authors.
The relevant upstream projects are Self-Forcing, Wan2.1, and FramePack.
- LightForcing-derived attention/selection primitives are identified in
  horizonkv/sparse_kernels.py and horizonkv/baseline_selector.py.
- The sparse attention implementation is based on the open-source
  Block-Sparse-Attention library, with modifications for HorizonKV:
  https://github.com/lemonadenn/Block-Sparse-Attention.git (fork of https://github.com/mit-han-lab/Block-Sparse-Attention.git)
  This modified backend is included in the HorizonKV package's
  third_party/Block-Sparse-Attention directory and
  supplies the 64x64 and variable-length paths used by HorizonKV.
  Retain its BSD license and the upstream notices on bundled kernel sources.

Upstream copyright and license notices are retained. No trained weights,
benchmark videos, experiment logs, development history, or author affiliation
information is distributed with this artifact. Downloaded model weights and
evaluation datasets remain subject to their respective licenses.

FlagScale integration (2026): inference modules have been moved into the
flagscale.inference.core.diffusion.horizonkv namespace. Research launchers,
ablation/reproduction scripts and the standalone CLI are excluded. Runtime
configuration and 14B model loading are owned by FlagScale. The modified
Block-Sparse-Attention dependency is at
FlagScale/flagscale/inference/core/diffusion/horizonkv/third_party/Block-Sparse-Attention.
